# Hello world (M4-2): the string goes to the standard output port directly (the port parameter
# is a static cell, the analysis proves it holds the open stdout); nothing allocates and nothing
# can raise, so neither the collector nor any exception machinery is linked.
fn P_init[(]
has rt_put_string[(]
has rt_put_newline[(]
no rt_display[(]
no rt_make_proc
no RT_PROC[(]
nm-no ^_?rt_alloc_slow$
nm-no ^_?gc_(run|mark|scan|refill|collect)
nm-no ^_?rt_(print|display|write|format_double|intern|read|open_input_file|make_error|raise|engine_raise|error|type_error|uncaught|fx_overflow)$
nm-no ^_?io_(scan|print|label|print_atom)$
nm-no ^_?P_scheme_base__
nm-no ^_?bn_
nm-has ^_?rt_port_write_fd$
nm-no ^_?(rt_call_cc|rt_call_cc3|core_rewind|core_reenter|core_callcc3_run|core_cont_code)$
